# Title: Suspicious File Write to SharePoint Layouts Directory
# ID: 1f0489be-b496-4ddf-b3a9-5900f2044e9c
# Status: experimental
# Level: high
# Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2025-07-24
# Tags: attack.initial-access, attack.t1190, attack.persistence, attack.t1505.003
# Description: Detects suspicious file writes to SharePoint layouts directory which could indicate webshell activity or post-exploitation.
# This behavior has been observed in the exploitation of SharePoint vulnerabilities such as CVE-2025-49704, CVE-2025-49706 or CVE-2025-53770.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((process.executable:*\\cmd.exe OR process.executable:*\\powershell_ise.exe OR process.executable:*\\powershell.exe OR process.executable:*\\pwsh.exe OR process.executable:*\\w3wp.exe) AND (file.path:C:\\Program Files\\Common Files\\Microsoft Shared\\Web Server Extensions\\* OR file.path:C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Common Files\\Microsoft Shared\\Web Server Extensions\\*) AND (file.path:*\\15\\TEMPLATE\\LAYOUTS\\* OR file.path:*\\16\\TEMPLATE\\LAYOUTS\\*) AND (file.path:*.asax OR file.path:*.ascx OR file.path:*.ashx OR file.path:*.asmx OR file.path:*.asp OR file.path:*.aspx OR file.path:*.bat OR file.path:*.cmd OR file.path:*.cer OR file.path:*.config OR file.path:*.hta OR file.path:*.js OR file.path:*.jsp OR file.path:*.jspx OR file.path:*.php OR file.path:*.ps1 OR file.path:*.vbs))
